        <li><strong>Obtuse Angles (90° &lt; θ &lt; 180°):</strong> Wide openings seen in reclining chairs, highway junctions, and obtuse triangles.</li>
        <li><strong>Straight Angles (θ = 180° or π rad):</strong> Collinear opposite rays that form a continuous straight line.</li>
        <li><strong>Reflex Angles (180° &lt; θ &lt; 360°):</strong> Exterior rotational angles used in mechanical cams, clock hands, and bearings.</li>
      </ul>
